From 675acf0e7bae35163f84250867bc533fe5d36bed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grizbeard <justin.morken@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:39:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] Draw skin-provided library icons without the selection
 tint

QIcon has no pixmap registered for QIcon::Selected, so QSvgIconEngine
renders one by blending the Normal pixmap 30% towards
QPalette::Highlight. That palette entry comes from the application
palette, which on Windows is seeded from the OS accent colour, so the
icon on the highlighted sidebar row was tinted towards a colour that has
nothing to do with the skin -- here a burnt orange over the sage the
skin had asked for.

The widget stylesheet cannot reach it: QIcon asks
QApplicationPrivate::applyQIconStyleHelper, which builds a bare
QStyleOption from qApp's palette rather than the sidebar's, so
selection-background-color on WLibrarySidebar has no effect.

Name the same file for the Selected mode as well. QSvgIconEngine only
generates a tinted variant when the mode it could load differs from the
one asked for, so an explicit entry makes it load the file directly and
the icon is drawn in the colour it was authored in. Disabled is left to
be generated, so disabled items still grey out.

Only skins that ship their own icons are affected; a skin using the
built-in icons keeps the previous behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/library/libraryfeature.cpp | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/library/libraryfeature.cpp b/src/library/libraryfeature.cpp
index 60095edf..964a74c7 100644
--- a/src/library/libraryfeature.cpp
+++ b/src/library/libraryfeature.cpp
@@ -66,8 +66,21 @@ LibraryFeature::LibraryFeature(
           m_iconName(iconName) {
     if (!m_iconName.isEmpty()) {
         const QString overridePath = skinIconPath(m_pConfig, m_iconName);
-        m_icon = QIcon(overridePath.isEmpty() ? kIconPath.arg(m_iconName)
-                                              : overridePath);
+        if (overridePath.isEmpty()) {
+            m_icon = QIcon(kIconPath.arg(m_iconName));
+        } else {
+            m_icon = QIcon(overridePath);
+            // QIcon generates the pixmap for a selected row by blending the
+            // Normal one 30% towards QPalette::Highlight, which on Windows is
+            // the OS accent colour and so is unrelated to the skin. Naming the
+            // file for the Selected mode as well makes QSvgIconEngine load it
+            // directly instead of generating a tinted variant, so an icon a
+            // skin ships is drawn in the colour it was authored in. Disabled
+            // is deliberately left to be generated, so disabled items still
+            // grey out.
+            m_icon.addFile(overridePath, QSize(), QIcon::Selected, QIcon::Off);
+            m_icon.addFile(overridePath, QSize(), QIcon::Selected, QIcon::On);
+        }
     }
 }
 
